# Act 2, chapter 5 "Siblings": Lapis and Lazuli, runaways in West City. Party: Lapis = character slot 1 (Gohan's),
# Lazuli = slot 3 (Trunks's). Started by a walk-in trigger at West City's arrival point (areas.json 4:1, active while
# flag 300 is clear); natives: 29 set flag, 151 join, 152 leave, 149 make player, 183 chapter card.
list ch5_start
do call 29 300
do call 151 1; call 151 3; call 149 1; call 152 0; call 152 2
# natives 164/165/166 (0xA4-0xA6) = add / remove / replace a skill in a character's list (record +0x0C). The twins start
# with Gohan's and Trunks's lists, which include Super Saiyan (skill 20): humans don't get that.
do call 165 1 20; call 165 3 20
# and keep them human: Lapis [7, 6, 17] (Energy Blast, Electric Kamehameha, Masenko) and Lazuli [7, 4, 11] (Energy
# Blast, Burning Attack, Flame Kamehameha) -> Energy Punch only. The procedure (chapter 6) gives the android moves.
do call 165 1 7; call 165 1 6; call 165 1 17; call 165 3 7; call 165 3 4; call 165 3 11
do call 164 1 8; call 164 3 8
do call 183 516 1458 1459
# after its card the Act 1 opening does: blank scene 0:2 (115), 121(1), 165(0, 20), then (in its packed type-4 step)
# 120(1) and 119(world, area, room, x, y) = load a field area with the player placed at (x, y); 120(n) / 121(n) =
# fade out / in over n frames
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1; call 165 0 20
do call 120 1; call 119 4 1 1 268 304; call 121 60
narrate Years later. West City.
say lapis.2 Three wallets, a wristwatch and a capsule case. Not bad for a Tuesday.
say lazuli.1 Not bad? You nearly tripped over that cop's shoelaces.
say lapis.2 Nearly. That's the important word.
say lazuli.0 Keep your voice down. That patrol car's been circling the block all morning.
say lapis.1 Then let's give them something to chase.
say lazuli.3 Fine. But if we get caught, I'm telling them it was your idea.
journal Explore West City
# end the cutscene and hand control back (the Act 1 opening's last step does the same)
do call 47; call 51 0
# West City townsfolk and police (Act 2), set on BF's own NPC objects via areas.json "object_talk"
list wc_woman_pink
narrate Townswoman: Hold on to your purse around here. A pair of kids has been picking pockets all week.
list wc_woman_blue
narrate Townswoman: Twins, people say. One dark-haired, one blonde... gone before you can blink.
list wc_man_green
# chapter 5 quest: the capsule case (flag 301)
if_flag 301 fence_done
narrate Fence: Psst. You two look like you've got something to sell.
say lapis.2 A capsule case. A fancy one. What's it worth to you?
narrate Fence: Let me see... Whoa. That's the Red Ribbon Army's mark inside the lid. Nobody's touching that.
narrate Fence: And kids... a man in a long coat was asking around about you two this morning. Very politely.
say lazuli.1 Great. Now we're famous.
set_flag 301
journal Find out who's asking about you
run ch5_check
stop
label fence_done
narrate Fence: I told you, I'm not touching that case. Get rid of it before it gets rid of you.
list wc_old_man
narrate Old man: Not so many years ago, the Red Ribbon Army marched right down this street.
narrate Old man: Then a single boy brought the whole army down. Or so the story goes.
list wc_police_1
narrate Police officer: Move along. We're looking for two runaways. Seen any kids who look like trouble?
list wc_police_2
narrate Police officer: The twins again! Third report today. When I catch them, they're spending the night at the station.
list wc_police_3
narrate Police officer: The chief wants patrols doubled. Those two keep slipping past every roadblock in town.
# chapter 5 quest: Hercule (flag 302)
list wc_hercule
if_flag 302 herc_done
narrate Hercule: Out of my way, kids! Future World Martial Arts Champion coming through!
say lazuli.3 Champion of what, the sidewalk?
narrate Hercule: Laugh now! One day the whole world will know my name. Hercule! Say it with me!
say lapis.2 Sure. We'll be waiting.
set_flag 302
run ch5_check
stop
label herc_done
unless_flag 461 herc_plain
if_flag 462 herc_plain
set_flag 462
say lazuli.1 Hercule. There's a crowd at the museum. A big one. And nobody there has ever heard of you.
narrate Hercule: NOBODY? That's an outrage! A tragedy! Stand aside, kids. Those people need a show!
narrate He jogs off toward the city hall steps, already shouting. A minute later the cheering starts.
say lapis.2 And every guard in that building is going to want to see what the noise is.
journal Slip into the museum storeroom while the guard is watching Hercule
stop
label herc_plain
narrate Hercule: Hah! Watch and learn, kids. Dynamite kick! ...Ow. My ankle.
# both quests done (and not run before) -> the end of chapter 5
list ch5_check
unless_flag 301 not_yet
unless_flag 302 not_yet
unless_flag 308 not_yet
unless_flag 295 not_yet
if_flag 303 not_yet
if_flag 460 not_yet
set_flag 460
say lazuli.0 That's everything, Lapis. Let's lie low at the warehouse till dark.
say lapis.1 Fine. But there's still daylight. Whatever we haven't done in town, now's the time.
journal Rest at the {c07}warehouse{c02} when you're ready (the chapter ends)
label not_yet
# the mattress heap in the old warehouse (examine): rest until night once everything is done (460)
list ch5_rest
unless_flag 460 rest_early
narrate The mattresses, dragged back where they belong. The twins settle in to wait for dark.
if_flag 467 rest_go
unless_flag 463 rest_go
set_flag 467
do call 130 28
narrate Lazuli wraps the Ribbon Ruby in a sock and puts it in the tin box, under the loose board.
say lapis.2 For later?
say lazuli.1 For later.
label rest_go
run ch5_end
stop
label rest_early
narrate Their old mattresses. There's no time to rest yet.
list ch5_end
set_flag 303
set_flag 337
say lazuli.0 Lapis. That man in the coat... the fence saw him, Big Ox took his money, I saw him on the bus. He's everywhere we go.
say lapis.1 Then we lie low. Back to the warehouse tonight. If he wants us that badly, let him come looking.
say lazuli.0 Fine. And Lapis? Ditch the case.
journal Hide out until nightfall
# -> chapter 6 "Taken": card, then West City at night (16:1, moonlit copy of 4:1), the twins in the park
do call 183 516 1460 1461
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1; call 165 0 20
do call 120 1; call 119 16 1 1 112 480; call 121 60
do call 29 304
narrate That night.
say lazuli.0 Every patrol in the city is out. And those flying things... what are they?
say lapis.1 Don't know. Don't care. Through the crossroads and down to the docks. Stay in the shadows.
narrate Out on the main road, the drones hang in a line, sweeping red beams across the street. Two more hover over the south bridge.
say lazuli.0 They've cut the city in half. Look, there's a gap in the beams, south of the crossroads.
say lapis.1 Our old house is on the other side. The roofs from there run all the way to the river.
journal Slip through the searchlights to your {c07}old house{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
# chapter 5 side job "Ditch the Patrol" (flag 307 chase running, 308 done): taunt the patrol cop, lose him in the park,
# and the man in the long coat (Gero) sees how good they are
list wc_cop_chase
if_flag 308 cop_done
if_flag 307 cop_running
narrate Police officer: Hold it! A wallet, a wristwatch and a capsule case went missing on this street today. Turn out your pockets.
say lapis.2 Officer, I'm offended. Do we look like thieves?
narrate Police officer: You look exactly like the two in the report!
say lazuli.3 Then he'll have to catch us first.
set_flag 307
do begin_moves; move patrol_cop 500 400; wait_moves
narrate Police officer: Stop! In the name of the West City Police!
say lapis.1 The park. We lose him in the trees.
journal Lose the cop in the park
# the script moved an actor: leave cutscene mode (without this the player stays locked)
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label cop_running
narrate Police officer: (wheezing) You... two... stop... running...
stop
label cop_done
narrate Police officer: You again. I know it was you. I just can't prove it.
list park_hide
unless_flag 307 hide_skip
if_flag 308 hide_skip
set_flag 308
say lazuli.0 Down. Behind the hedge.
do begin_moves; move patrol_cop 230 380; wait_moves
narrate Police officer: ...Lost them. Again. The chief is going to have my badge.
do begin_moves; move patrol_cop 700 400; wait_moves
do begin_moves; move player_gero_106 600 400; wait_moves
do begin_moves; move player_gero_106 270 396; wait_moves
narrate Across the street, a man in a long coat watches the hedge for a long moment. Then he writes something down.
say lapis.2 Too easy.
say lazuli.0 Lapis... who's that?
journal You lost the cop. Somebody else was watching.
do call 47; call 51 0
run ch5_check
stop
label hide_skip
list wc_coat_man
if_flag 308 coat_after
narrate Man in a long coat: Hm? Run along, children.
stop
label coat_after
narrate Man in a long coat: Quick. Clever. And nobody looking after you at all... Remarkable.
# ---------- chapter 6 "Taken" (flags 304 opening seen, 305 ambush done, 306 conversion done = outfit swap unlocked)
list night_police
narrate Police officer: Curfew's in effect, kids. Nobody on the streets after dark. Not with those machines flying around.
list night_drone
narrate The machine hums overhead. A red eye sweeps slowly across the street.
say lazuli.0 Don't move. Don't even breathe.
# walk-in trigger at the crossroads (16:1): the drones close in, a voice, a flash -> the lab
list ch6_ambush
set_flag 305
# 16:44 (the warehouse after the Collector, gen_ch6.py): the player arrives at (150,176), the drones close in
narrate The machine shudders and goes dark. In the silence, a hum. Then another. Then a third.
say lazuli.0 Wait. Listen.
do begin_moves; move drone_night_a 150 136; move drone_night_b 196 176; move drone_night_c 104 176; wait_moves
say lapis.1 Those aren't police drones.
narrate Voice: Subjects located. Seventeen and Eighteen. Do not damage them.
say lazuli.0 Seventeen? Who are you calling...
say lapis.1 Lazuli, run!
narrate A white flash. Then nothing.
do call 120 30
do call 120 1; call 119 1 66 1 150 228; call 121 90
narrate Dr. Gero's Laboratory.
say gero Lapis. Lazuli. You were not easy to find.
say lazuli.0 Let us go, you creep! Who do you think you are?
say gero The man who will make you perfect. Your old names end tonight. From now on you are Seventeen and Eighteen.
say lapis.1 Lazuli... whatever he does to us, stay close.
do call 120 60
# the outfit swap unlocks (skill 18, BF's Saiyaman, re-pointed by tools/outfit.py) and both wake in the android
# outfit: 157(c, actor idx) picks the first form whose +0xE = actor idx (actor id + 9): 111 = actor 102 -> form 14
# (Android 17), 271 = actor 262 -> form 23 (Android 18).
# 1:79 is the same tank room with Lazuli's NPC as 18.
# 165 with skill id 240 (0xF0) = android upgrade (tools/outfit.py hook_rm): STR/POW +22, END +18, SPD +12, HP +230, EP +70
do call 164 1 7; call 164 1 6; call 164 3 7; call 164 3 6; call 164 3 4
do call 164 1 18; call 164 3 18; call 157 1 111; call 157 3 271; call 165 1 240; call 165 3 240
do call 119 1 79 1 150 228; call 121 60
narrate The procedure took eleven days.
narrate When the twins opened their eyes, the world looked different. Sharper. Smaller. Easy to break.
set_flag 306
journal Lapis and Lazuli are gone
narrate New skill: Outfit. Select it and press the B Button to switch between the android clothes and the old ones.
run ch7_start
list gero_lab_talk
say gero Rest while you can. Your first tests begin tomorrow.
list lazuli_lab_talk
say lazuli.0 Eighteen. He keeps calling me Eighteen. The worst part is how easy it is to answer to it.
